input fold-skip warnings |\n| discussion-excerpt.txt | the 0.1.5-alpha.1 round of the same failure family (discussion #5999) |\n--- symptom-log ---\n# Symptom log — dsh 0.1.5-alpha.2, Windows 11, npm-global in-place upgrade\n# (profile created under 0.1.2/0.1.3; six external client plugins junction-linked)\n\n## Timeline\n\n1. npm i -g @deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.5-alpha.2, then dsh web restart.\n   Boot output: \"[dsh-profiles] ready\", web URL printed. No visible errors in the terminal.\n\n2. Clicking a chat file link whose address is OUTSIDE the session workspace:\n\n   sidebarRight: no registered tab type claims\n   \"dsh-resource://file/absolute/E:/deepseek-harness/dsh-input-history/package.json\"\n\n   (dialog: 无法打开文件 / 重试)\n\n3. The assistant then writes a test file INSIDE the session workspace:\n\n   E:\\deepseek-harness\\test-lhh010\\.dsh\\tmp\\sidebar-open-test-2.md\n\n   Clicking THAT link opens a right-Sidebar tab titled \"sidebar-open-test-2.md\" —\n   progress over the earlier dialog. But the tab's content area shows only:\n\n   文件资源服务不可用。\n\n   No error message, no retry hint. The file-trace plugin's own RPC reads the same\n   file fine in its panel (原文/阅读 modes both show the content).\n\n4. F12 Console: no red errors from documentpreview or the sidebar; the only warnings\n   are from dsh-paste-input (\"fold skipped (parse failed)\" — see console-excerpt.txt).\n\n5. Per-module probe of all 62 manifest entries (see combo-probe.txt): every one returns\n   HTTP 200. Zero 404s.\n--- boot-manifest ---\n# Boot manifest excerpt (__DSH_BOOT__, fetched same-origin after the restart)\n# Total entries: 60. Relevant rows verbatim:\n\n{\"id\":\"@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-workspace-files\",\"url\":\"/plugins/??@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-workspace-files/client.js&rev=234716e8f7370214-3\",\"inject\":[\"@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-gateway\",\"@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-resources\"]}\n\n{\"id\":\"@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-sidebar-right\",\"url\":\"/plugins/??@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-sidebar-right/client.js&rev=234716e8f7370214-N\"}\n\n# Sidebar package census (plain substring counts over the whole HTML):\n#   ui-sidebar-right        -> present\n#   ui-sidebar-textpreview  -> ABSENT (0 mentions)\n#   ui-sidebar-documentpreview -> the 0.1.5-alpha.2 tree REPLACED\n#       packages/client/ui-sidebar-textpreview with\n#       packages/client/ui-sidebar-documentpreview\n#       (packages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml carries the\n#        ui-sidebar-documentpreview row; the old ui-sidebar-textpreview row is gone)\n#   dsh-file-trace   -> present (all six external plugins present)\n#   dsh-profiles     -> present\n#   dsh-brand-version -> present\n\n# Note: the text tab type (\"text\", claiming dsh-resource://file/**) was registered by\n# ui-sidebar-textpreview in 0.1.5-alpha.1. In 0.1.5-alpha.2 the replacement package\n# ui-sidebar-documentpreview registers a document tab whose canOpen accepts\n# parseFileAddress(address)?.scope === 'session' only.\n--- combo-probe ---\n# Combo / per-module probes on the running 0.1.5-alpha.2 host (no auth needed for\n# the /plugins/?? route).\n\n## Probe 1 — the boot manifest's first combo URL (single module):\n\nGET /plugins/??@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-gateway/client.js&rev=234716e8f7370214-0\n→ 200, 73 616 bytes. (Serves correctly.)\n\n## Probe 2 — all 62 entries joined into one URL:\n\nGET /plugins/??<62 modules comma-joined>&rev=234716e8f7370214-0\n→ 404, zero-length body. The joined URL is ~4–5 KB long.\n\n## Probe 3 — per-module sweep: all 62 manifest entries fetched one by one:\n\n→ 62/62 HTTP 200, zero 404s.\n--- contrast-probe ---\n# Contrast probe — two readers, same file, same moment\n\nFile: E:\\deepseek-harness\\test-lhh010\\.dsh\\tmp\\sidebar-open-test-2.md\n      (session-scoped address:\n       dsh-resource://file/session/session-2844c12c-5870-41e0-bb46-7d1fdc7c183a/.dsh/tmp/sidebar-open-test-2.md)\n\n| Reader | Transport | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| file-trace plugin (own host RPC, /dsh-file-trace/* routes) | its own HTTP face | READS FINE — 原文 and 阅读 modes both show the content |\n| documentpreview sidebar tab | api-workspace-files Remote | FAILS — meta.status stays 'none', the tab shows 文件资源服务不可用。 |\n\nHost-side notes (0.1.5-alpha.2 tree):\n- The workspace-files host row IS in the web-app bundle patch\n  (cordis.patch.yml: \"- id: workspace-files / name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-workspace-files'\").\n- The service resolves each session's workspace root via a typert lookups.register entry\n  (sessions.get(sessionId)?.header.cwd, falling back to sandboxPolicy.workspaceRoot).\n- Files OUTSIDE the session workspace are allowed (\"files outside it are allowed\" —\n  index.ts read() doc), so .dsh/tmp being under the workspace root is not the blocker.\n--- console ---\n# Browser console excerpt (F12) on the failing page\n\n[dsh-profiles:client] ready                                    client.js:208\n\n[Deprecation]-ms-high-contrast-adjust is in the process of being deprecated…\n[Deprecation]-ms-high-contrast-adjust is in the process of being deprecated…\n[新] 通过在 Microsoft Edge 中使用 Copilot 来解释控制台错误：…（不再显示）\n[Deprecation]-ms-high-contrast-adjust is in the process of being deprecated…\n\n▲ dsh-paste-input: fold skipped (parse failed): - client.js:1010\n  The attachment message protocol (the ```\n  ==== DSH_PASTE_INPUT_V1 ====` marker) and the\n  `.dsh/tmp/attachments/<session>/<send>/` directory logic do not\n  depend on snapshot-internal implementation details; the full chain\n  was verified successfully in practice on 0809.\n▲ dsh-paste-input: fold skipped (parse failed): - client.js:1010\n  **Bubble collapsing**: after sending, the verbose attachment-path\n  text block in the message bubble (carrying the ```\n  ==== DSH_PASTE_INPUT_V1 ====` marker protocol) is automatically collapsed\n  into a 📎 file chip; …\n… (repeats for every historical paste-attachment message)\n\n# (no other console output captured on the failing page)\n--- discussion ---\n# Prior art — the same failure family on 0.1.5-alpha.1 (2026-09-09)\n\ndeepseek-ai/deepseek-harness discussion #5999\n(https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions/5999)\ndocuments the 0.1.5-alpha.1 round of the same failure family on this deployment:\n\n- An npm-global in-place upgrade onto a profile created under 0.1.2/0.1.3 left the\n  client roster and the served combo inconsistent: the boot roster listed the\n  newly-added ui-sidebar-* modules but the combo route answered 404 for them at the\n  same rev (old modules 200 at that rev) — so every client plugin failed with\n  \"loaded without registering\" (the first unregistered entry, client-hmr, named\n  innocently).\n- A host restart self-healed the roster/combo mismatch once (the newly-added rows\n  entered the roster), but the sidebar tab's content read STILL failed on that boot\n  (文件资源服务不可用) — the resource-provider chain did not take over.\n- Rollback to the previous published version (npm i -g @deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.3-alpha.2)\n  was verified as the escape hatch.\n\nThe 0.1.5-alpha.2 round on the same profile shows a related-but-narrower symptom:\nmodules serve individually (62/62 probes 200), the documentpreview tab opens, but the\nfile resource metadata still never arrives. The forensics were appended to #5999 as\nround 2 (comment 18371079).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
